# Scripts that CI executes on Linux must keep LF endings regardless of the
# committer's platform. This repo is developed on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF shebang makes Linux fail the whole script with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" -- a failure mode with no useful error message.
*.sh text eol=lf
formalization/QuerySystem/blueprint/bin/kpsewhich text eol=lf
